</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     2. CURRENT GMT AND PDT TIME
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->


<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     3. WHAT IS PACIFIC DAYLIGHT TIME?
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section reveal" id="what-is-pdt">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">TimeZone Definition</div>
    <h2>What is Pacific Daylight Time?</h2>
    <p>
      Pacific Daylight Time (PDT) is the timezone offset used along the North American Pacific Coast (UTC-7) during the summer months.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is active from the second Sunday of March, when clocks spring forward from PST, to the first Sunday of November, when clocks fall back.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     4. UNDERSTANDING UTC-7
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section reveal" id="understanding-utc-7">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">Offset Mechanics</div>
    <h2>Understanding UTC-7</h2>
    <p>
      UTC-7 represents Coordinated Universal Time minus 7 hours. This offset runs along the Pacific Coast of North America, including major municipal and commercial centers in California, Oregon, and Washington.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     5. GMT VS PDT
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section reveal" id="gmt-vs-pdt">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">Standard Clarifications</div>
    <h2>GMT vs PDT</h2>
    <p>
      Greenwich Mean Time (GMT) is a solar-based baseline timezone that remains constant year-round. Pacific Daylight Time (PDT) is the summer daylight timezone for the Pacific Coast.
    </p>
    <p>
      During summer, PDT is exactly 7 hours behind GMT. In winter, when the region returns to Pacific Standard Time (PST), the gap increases to 8 hours.
    </p>
  </div>
  
  <!-- SVG 2: GMT → PDT TIMELINE -->
  <div class="hero-visual" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 24px auto 0;">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 800 180" width="100%" height="auto" style="background: #0f172a; border-radius: 8px;">
      <text x="400" y="35" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">GMT VS PDT SEASONAL TIMELINE OFFSET</text>
      <line x1="80" y1="100" x2="720" y2="100" stroke="#2f6278" stroke-width="4" />
      
      <!-- GMT Node -->
      <circle cx="200" cy="100" r="10" fill="#36c7b5" />
      <text x="200" y="75" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">GMT (UTC+0)</text>
      <text x="200" y="130" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#bdd2dc" text-anchor="middle">Greenwich Meridian</text>

      <!-- PDT Node -->
      <circle cx="600" cy="100" r="10" fill="#8fd7ff" />
      <text x="600" y="75" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">PDT (UTC-7)</text>
      <text x="600" y="130" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#bdd2dc" text-anchor="middle">Pacific Coast (Summer)</text>

      <path d="M 200 100 L 200 115 L 600 115 L 600 100" fill="none" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.5" />
      <text x="400" y="150" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#8fd7ff" text-anchor="middle">8-Hour Winter Gap (PST) | 7-Hour Summer Gap (PDT)</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     DEDICATED SECTION: PDT VS PST
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section reveal" id="pdt-vs-pst-use">
