      Selecting between PDT and PST depends entirely on the date of your conversion:
    </p>
    <ul style="margin: 16px 0 0; padding-left: 1.5rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7;">
      <li><strong>Use Pacific Daylight Time (PDT, UTC-7)</strong>: From the second Sunday of March to the first Sunday of November, during the summer months.</li>
      <li><strong>Use Pacific Standard Time (PST, UTC-8)</strong>: From the first Sunday of November to the second Sunday of March, during the winter months.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Our dynamic timezone calculator handles these transitions automatically, ensuring you calculate offsets correctly.
    </p>
  </div>
  
  <!-- SVG 5: PDT VS PST COMPARISON -->
