<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     14. WHEN PDT STARTS AND ENDS
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section reveal" id="when-pdt">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">DST Transitions</div>
    <h2>When PDT Starts and Ends</h2>
    <p>
      In the United States and Canada, PDT begins on the second Sunday of March, when clocks spring forward one hour from PST (UTC-8) to PDT (UTC-7).
    </p>
    <p>
      PDT ends on the first Sunday of November, when clocks fall back one hour from PDT (UTC-7) to PST (UTC-8).
    </p>
  </div>
  
